Regional Market Insights
•	India: India stands as the powerhouse within the Asia-Pacific Motorcycle Market, driven by its massive population, rapid urbanization, and acute traffic congestion that favors compact two-wheelers. A burgeoning middle class fuels demand for affordable commuter bikes, while rural areas sustain high-volume sales. Government initiatives like FAME subsidies accelerate electric adoption.
•	China: China plays a critical role, leveraging manufacturing prowess for both domestic and export markets. Urban pollution controls spur premium and electric variants, with government policies favoring low-emission vehicles and battery innovations.
•	Southeast Asia (Indonesia, Thailand, Vietnam): Diverse needs favor durable scooters amid congested cities and tropical climates. Rising middle classes, e-commerce logistics, and EV incentives drive growth, supported by local assembly.
•	Japan: Excels through technological superiority in performance and adventure models, catering to enthusiasts amid aging demographics and strong exports.
•	Australia & New Zealand: Niche focus on safety, leisure, and touring bikes, with electric traction and premium imports among affluent consumers.
